# File: tests/unit/test_unreal_import.py
# Generated from: specs/141-fix-import-ue-failing-multi-part-static-imports-because-ue-5-8-reports-only-the-first-mesh-on-the-import-task/requirements.md
Feature: import_ue resolves imported meshes from the destination folder

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: A multi-part static import returns every part
    Given a Crate snapshot with parts SM_Crate, SM_Crate_Body, and SM_Crate_Lid
    And a fake import that creates all three Static Meshes in the destination folder
    When the generated import code runs
    Then NMG_RESULT is ok with three static_meshes entries

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Expected meshes are resolved by name, ignoring other assets
    Given a fake import task that lists only the first mesh, and a folder that also holds an unrelated Static Mesh
    When the generated import code runs
    Then each expected part is resolved from the folder by name
    And the unrelated mesh is neither bound nor reported

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: A rigged Desktop import creates a missing physics asset
    Given a rigged Crate whose Desktop import created SM_Crate and SM_Crate_Skeleton but no physics asset
    When the generated Desktop import code runs
    Then create_physics_asset is called for SM_Crate
    And SM_Crate_PhysicsAsset exists in the Desktop folder, is assigned to SM_Crate, and is saved
    And NMG_RESULT is ok

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: A rigged Mobile import reuses the Desktop rig assets
    Given a Desktop folder holding SM_Crate_Skeleton and SM_Crate_PhysicsAsset
    When the generated Mobile import code runs
    Then the import options use the Desktop skeleton and physics asset
    And LOD 1 and LOD 2 are imported
    And NMG_RESULT is ok

  @SCN005
  Scenario: A re-import reports the new geometry
    Given a folder that already holds SM_Crate from an earlier import
    When a fake import replaces SM_Crate with new bounds
    Then the reported bounds are the new ones
    And the pivot check passes against the new snapshot

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Every missing part is named
    Given a fake import after which SM_Crate_Body and SM_Crate_Lid are absent
    When import_variant runs the generated code
    Then it raises import_ue.failed naming SM_Crate_Body and SM_Crate_Lid

  @SCN007 @regression
  Scenario: Two-part regression with an under-reporting task
    Given a two-part static Crate whose fake task lists only the first mesh, while both part assets exist
    When the generated import code runs against the fake unreal module
    Then NMG_RESULT is ok with both parts in static_meshes

  @SCN008
  Scenario: A single-part import behaves as before
    Given a single-part static Crate
    When the generated import code runs against the fake unreal module
    Then texture settings, MI_Crate_Body binding, the NMG_RESULT keys, and the pivot check match the existing behavior

  @SCN009
  Scenario: The Interchange cvar is not offered as a workaround
    Given the repository's src, skills, docs, scripts, and templates
    When they are scanned
    Then none contains Interchange.FeatureFlags.Import.FBX
    And the generated import code does not reference it
